/S /H2
/T (AI privacy is currently failing in both of these arenas: opaque personalization practices and ambiguous biometric law. Future efforts could focus on clear statutes for biometrics along with controllable personalization, and if the RAI and Privacy communities succeed in hard-wiring these principles into legislation, procurement, and assurance, then AI systems will be demonstrably and significantly more privacy-preserving. )
/E (AI privacy is currently failing in both of these arenas: opaque personalization practices and ambiguous biometric law. Future efforts could focus on clear statutes for biometrics along with controllable personalization, and if the RAI and Privacy communities succeed in hard-wiring these principles into legislation, procurement, and assurance, then AI systems will be demonstrably and significantly more privacy-preserving. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
